WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.700
(banjo music)

00:00:01.700 --> 00:00:03.710
- People don't realize,
when they walk outside,

00:00:03.710 --> 00:00:06.360
there's basically a grocery
store surrounding them.

00:00:06.360 --> 00:00:08.493
And that's such a beautiful
thing about nature.

00:00:09.750 --> 00:00:12.510
A lot of my job is to
walk around in the woods

00:00:12.510 --> 00:00:13.730
and say, oh, what is that in the ground?

00:00:13.730 --> 00:00:15.428
Pick it up and eat it.

00:00:15.428 --> 00:00:17.000
I have this sort of curious nature

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:18.920
where I never am satisfied with something.

00:00:18.920 --> 00:00:21.530
If we're cooking something,
how can we do it better?

00:00:21.530 --> 00:00:23.380
How can you make it more interesting?

00:00:24.440 --> 00:00:25.900
We have to eat, as human beings,

00:00:25.900 --> 00:00:28.600
so why not make it the most
memorable experience you can?

00:00:35.110 --> 00:00:38.300
My name is James Gop.
I'm a culinary artist,

00:00:38.300 --> 00:00:40.683
forager, and founder of Heirloom Fire.

00:00:42.020 --> 00:00:44.450
More often than not, we're
working with clients,

00:00:44.450 --> 00:00:45.870
executing their vision.

00:00:45.870 --> 00:00:48.520
So, I'm incredibly
flattered that Coors Light

00:00:48.520 --> 00:00:49.640
wants to let us create a dinner

00:00:49.640 --> 00:00:51.690
that we'll be doing later this week

00:00:51.690 --> 00:00:54.270
where we are building
a menu designed around

00:00:54.270 --> 00:00:57.600
native species, what's
growing in that moment.

00:00:57.600 --> 00:00:58.540
The Berkshires have a little bit

00:00:58.540 --> 00:01:00.510
of a reputation for a reason.

00:01:00.510 --> 00:01:01.890
We're a little bit more north,

00:01:01.890 --> 00:01:04.090
so the growing seasons are so short.

00:01:04.090 --> 00:01:06.910
So it's really about
embracing that moment in time.

00:01:06.910 --> 00:01:10.133
Viewing it as, when the iron's
hot, you have to strike.

00:01:11.950 --> 00:01:14.670
- [Chris] The thing about
James is he never stops.

00:01:14.670 --> 00:01:16.150
- Chris, look at this, man.

00:01:16.150 --> 00:01:18.790
All the wild grape vines.

00:01:18.790 --> 00:01:20.527
Should you, just like
we've been talking about.

00:01:20.527 --> 00:01:22.430
It even has a sweet quality to it.

00:01:22.430 --> 00:01:25.900
- He holds himself at such a high standard

00:01:25.900 --> 00:01:28.290
that when he gets to where his dream is,

00:01:28.290 --> 00:01:30.330
his own standard goes up.

00:01:30.330 --> 00:01:31.580
That's very inspiring, in a way,

00:01:31.580 --> 00:01:33.540
because it pushes you to
just continue to be better,

00:01:33.540 --> 00:01:36.023
just continue to be better,
and continue to be better.

00:01:37.060 --> 00:01:38.440
- [James] My largest form of inspiration

00:01:38.440 --> 00:01:39.510
is going into woods.

00:01:39.510 --> 00:01:41.250
It makes me feel like this warmth in my chest

00:01:41.250 --> 00:01:42.870
and the hair stand up
on the back of my neck,

00:01:42.870 --> 00:01:45.190
and I want to be able to
share that with people.

00:01:45.190 --> 00:01:47.060
That's my artistic expression,

00:01:47.060 --> 00:01:49.363
to be able to replicate
that moment in time.

00:01:54.150 --> 00:01:56.730
It's usually about a 17-hour day onsite.

00:01:56.730 --> 00:01:58.790
It's a big experience
where you have to love it.

00:01:58.790 --> 00:02:01.440
And thankfully, I have that in a team.

00:02:01.440 --> 00:02:03.150
So we're onsite now.

00:02:03.150 --> 00:02:05.480
I'm hoping, today, to
get a hold of some stuff

00:02:05.480 --> 00:02:08.893
we weren't able to get due to
the massive rain last night.

00:02:10.100 --> 00:02:14.960
Wow, this is the first hen
of the woods I've ever found.

00:02:14.960 --> 00:02:17.960
We'll break off all the little 
sort of petals here

00:02:17.960 --> 00:02:20.770
and just sauté them in a lot
of butter and a lot of salt

00:02:20.770 --> 00:02:22.870
and just fold them in with the vegetables.

00:02:26.050 --> 00:02:27.160
- So I was out in the woods;

00:02:27.160 --> 00:02:29.310
came across these little red berries

00:02:29.310 --> 00:02:31.430
that taste remarkably like black pepper.

00:02:31.430 --> 00:02:33.323
- Let's put them in a dish tonight.

00:02:39.881 --> 00:02:40.860
Hello, everyone.

00:02:40.860 --> 00:02:42.980
Thank you very much for coming.

00:02:42.980 --> 00:02:45.693
My goal is to, really, forever
change your lives today.

00:02:46.550 --> 00:02:48.700
I want to have everybody take this moment

00:02:48.700 --> 00:02:51.420
where they're just being here, present,

00:02:51.420 --> 00:02:54.300
and realizing that these
aren't just weeds and grasses,

00:02:54.300 --> 00:02:55.980
but looking around and thinking of, wow,

00:02:55.980 --> 00:02:58.803
that's actually like an edible
grocery store out there.

00:03:00.730 --> 00:03:02.370
I love the theater of what we do.

00:03:02.370 --> 00:03:04.530
That's something that I want
to be able to give people.

00:03:04.530 --> 00:03:06.060
The theater, the entertainment,

00:03:06.060 --> 00:03:08.790
exposing them to something
they've never seen.

00:03:08.790 --> 00:03:10.190
Really, having a moment in life

00:03:10.190 --> 00:03:12.080
that people are gonna walk away from,

00:03:12.080 --> 00:03:14.860
and it'll be a memory that's
burned inside of them forever.

00:03:14.860 --> 00:03:17.060
As you see, obviously, there's
ice cream involved here,

00:03:17.060 --> 00:03:18.550
but this is birchwood ice cream.

00:03:18.550 --> 00:03:21.180
It's made by infusing
slices of birchwood,

00:03:21.180 --> 00:03:23.800
and cream, milk and sugar overnight.

00:03:23.800 --> 00:03:25.180
And if you look above you,

00:03:25.180 --> 00:03:27.030
we've actually foraged pine bark,

00:03:27.030 --> 00:03:29.500
and then put it into whole wheat flower.

00:03:29.500 --> 00:03:31.133
So these are little beignets.

00:03:33.040 --> 00:03:34.540
Did you enjoy everything?

00:03:34.540 --> 00:03:35.930
- Absolutely.
- Yeah?

00:03:35.930 --> 00:03:37.220
Great.
(crowd clapping)

00:03:37.220 --> 00:03:38.810
Great.

00:03:38.810 --> 00:03:40.440
Thank you, again, for making time.

00:03:40.440 --> 00:03:43.590
Sincerely, it really
means everything to us

00:03:43.590 --> 00:03:46.053
that you come and be a
part of this experience.

00:03:46.053 --> 00:03:47.810
I just want to open your
eyes back to nature,

00:03:47.810 --> 00:03:49.940
because there's so much
that we've forgotten.

00:03:49.940 --> 00:03:52.120
So thank you again for all coming,

00:03:52.120 --> 00:03:54.500
and I just want to take a
moment to thank Coors Light

00:03:54.500 --> 00:03:57.360
for giving us the opportunity
to tell our story.

00:03:57.360 --> 00:03:58.352
Cheers.

00:03:58.352 --> 00:03:59.951
(crowd cheering)

00:03:59.951 --> 00:04:02.868
(bottles rattling)

